    "body": "Like this, and I also think use `windowfeatures` is better than a \"_split\" target.\n\n\n> 2\\. I like this.\n>     But I don't quite understand how this is supposed to work if one is already in a split view. Say you're in the left view and try to open a new view in the bottom.  A browser might support only  either vertical or horizontal split at a time.\n>     And splitsize is likely a bit problematic. Browser window might be very narrow, in that case splitsize=20 would be probably very unusable - in such case 50 would make more sense. But on a wide screen, 20 could be totally fine.\n\n- [If the window is already split, the request falls back to a new tab.](https://github.com/mfreed7/split-tabs/blob/cb615ab81dabce94fc0dc9df11ef72d10782e4ee/README.md?plain=1#L201)\n- The user agent may ignore `split`, `splitposition`, and/or `splitsize` entirely — for example on a narrow\n  window, on mobile, or based on user settings. It may also clamp `splitsize` to a usable range. [Ref](https://github.com/mfreed7/split-tabs/blob/cb615ab81dabce94fc0dc9df11ef72d10782e4ee/README.md?plain=1#L184-L187)",
