    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T19:55:58Z",
    "body": "> Thanks for the proposal, I really like it. I also believe the AI agent use case is an important one: agents keep opening pages, and splits would keep the conversation visible beside them instead of losing it behind tab switches.\n\nThanks for the feedback and testing!\n\n\n\n> So pane reuse with existing mechanics depends entirely on the opened site's COOP policy.\n> \n> _Questions:_ Would it make sense for panes opened via `split` to stay replaceable, or to define a replace mechanism? And should the explainer mention this interaction?\n\nThis is a great point, thanks for pointing it out. I've added a section to the explainer that touches on this:\n\n- https://github.com/mfreed7/split-tabs#reusing-a-split-after-a-coop-navigation\n\nTL;DR I think we shouldn't try to change COOP to get around this limitation, it's inherently what COOP is trying to protect against.",
